        </figure>
      </question>

      <remark>
        <p>
          We will see in <xref ref="dimension-basis-colspace-dim"/> that the dimension of the span of the columns is equal to the number of pivots of <m>A</m>.  That is, the columns of <m>A</m> span a line if <m>A</m> has one pivot, they span a plane if <m>A</m> has two pivots, etc.  The whole space <m>\R^m</m> has dimension <m>m</m>, so this generalizes the fact that the columns of <m>A</m> span <m>\R^m</m> when <m>A</m> has <m>m</m> pivots.
        </p>
      </remark>

    </paragraphs>

  </subsection>

</section>
